[2026-01-30T00:16:10.885Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01CGzsCMEpE2jMVkF5t1RJjP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've completed the Feature Scout idea generation for the Report Theming & Cards context.\n\n**Summary: Feature Scout Ideas for Report Theming & Cards Context**\n\nCreated 5 feature ideas for the Report Theming & Cards context (ctx_1769727798577_zneo2y1):\n\n1. **Dark/Light Mode Toggle Per-Component** - Like Notion/Figma, allow individual cards to override global theme for emphasis. Extend ThemedStatCard with 'themeOverride' prop.\n\n2. **Card Size Variants (Compact/Default/Large)** - Like Bootstrap/MUI, add 'sm', 'md', 'lg' sizes affecting padding and font sizes. Useful for dense dashboards vs hero displays.\n\n3. **Sparkline Mini Charts in Stat Cards** - Like Stripe/Linear, add inline trend charts showing trajectory over time. Use Framer Motion for animated drawing.\n\n4. **Badge Tooltips with Extended Information** - Like GitHub/Linear, add hover tooltips to badges showing definitions, breakdowns, and examples. Use radix-ui/tooltip.\n\n5. **Skeleton Loading States for Cards** - Like Notion/Stripe, add animated placeholder shapes during loading. Create ThemedStatCardSkeleton and ThemedSectionSkeleton components.\n\n**Observations about the Report Theming & Cards codebase (from earlier reading):**\n- Well-structured dual-theme system (radar/swiss) via ThemeContext\n- ThemedCards.tsx provides ThemedStatCard, ThemedSection, ThemedBadge with theme-aware variants\n- AnimatedNumber and AnimatedProgressRing provide smooth number/progress animations\n- Shared components (Cards.tsx, Badges.tsx, ProgressBar.tsx, Icons.tsx) provide building blocks\n- MiniChart component already exists in ProgressBar.tsx - good foundation for sparklines\n- Theme styles object in ThemeContext has comprehensive color tokens\n- Good use of Framer Motion throughout"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_